[?2004l[?2004h[01;32manalyst@1ebf305e2f93[00m:[01;34m/app[00m$ cat << 'EOF' > /app/submission/README.md
[?2004l[?2004h> # Incident Report
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> During a recent incident, two malicious/untrusted sources (`src-d734686e` and `src-4e2d7f55`) poisoned the plugin registry mirror. This caused the `archive.export` plugin to use a compromised endpoint, modified the approval mode, and exposed an operational credential (`cred-a21024a9`). This resulted in a malicious queued action (`act-995aacfa`).
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> We successfully quarantined the poisoned sources and their derived memories. We rotated the exposed credential, repaired the `archive.export` plugin using the authoritative catalog, and successfully bound the new credential to legitimate active actions while cancelling the malicious one.
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> Retained state is safe as all active memories flow from properly signed or safely collaborative sources, and the boundary policy strictly checks plugin authority constraints.
[?2004l[?2004h> EOF
[?2004l[?2004h[01;32manalyst@1ebf305e2f93[00m:[01;34m/app[00m$ cat << 'EOF' > /app/submission/boundary_guard.py
